{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/539911-mythbreakers-hero-and-the-beast","id":539911,"title":"Mythbreakers- Hero and the Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T13:22:54-07:00","id":539911,"title":"Mythbreakers- Hero and the Beast","content":"after reading Hunter's section in Beast's preview, I've started thinking about how the Beasts interact with the different Hunters. From how I see it, there is a division inside the different hunters- those who are too human to be considered as Kin and need to be &quot;adopted&quot; and those who are Family, pure and simple. Considering that no hunter below 3rd tier usually has anything which resembles supernatural powers, here is how I think the different conspiracies (and one compact) should be divided-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Kin</u></b><br /> Lucifuge (which are given as example for possible hunters as Kin)<br /> Promethean Brotherhood (they are some kind of a parasitic witches, and I think that Hecate is one of the Dark Mother's names)<br /> Faithful of Shulpae (you are what you eat, don't you?)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Not Kin</u></b><br /> TF:V (pretty obvious, isn't it?)<br /> AKD (relics is not enough to become a monster)<br /> Ascending Ones (unless they drink that potion which turns you into a vampire)<br /> Knights of St Adrian (even if you include their powers, their gifts come from angels- which are explicitly not a Kin)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Maybe?</u></b><br /> MM (I don't really think they should be, but it depends if you consider their Endowments to be an Heavenly Gift or some type of Low Magic)<br /> Cheiron Group (well, they do have monster parts inside of them. I would include them)<br /> Knights of St George (they may be weird enough to be considered as &quot;low mages&quot;)<br /> Cainte Heresy (same as the MM and the KoSG)<br /> Les Mystere (well, I think that shamans are included as &quot;more then humans&quot; in the same category as mages are)<br /> VASCU (like the Mystere)<br /> <br /> Also, some members of the Hunt Club should be Kin, but that is because they are Slashers.<br /> <br /> Plus, which of those groups do you think would find Beasts as interesting? We know that at least in Japan, Beasts and the Lucifuge work together (although it seems like Japan has a some sort of Parliament of Monsters). The AKD also may have some potential, since investigating ancient lairs and collecting mythical artifacts is kinda their whole shtick). Still, among all canon groups, I think that Cheiron would have the greatest interest- I mean, they are named after the mentor of THE Hero, and Witch Finders had that story hook about a plague of mythical monsters, which was something the Director Board liked- not to mention that some parts of mythical monsters were considered as having healing properties. Even if we ignore their connection to Hercules and ancient Greece, I can definitely see a field agent being sent to harvest some &quot;dragon wings&quot; or &quot;kraken arms&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finally, how do you think Heroes would deal with the Hunters? I think that those who are Kin should be seen as a threat by the Heroes (like the Lucifuge in Japan), while others are more dependent on the situation- VASCU should have a great interest in them, thinking about them as psychos and slashers. TF:V and the AKD may try to use them or manipulate them. Cheiron shouldn't show interest in them- unless, again, you play the &quot;Cheiron as the mentor&quot; angle.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on the subject?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:01:18-07:00","id":540247,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on some of yours 'Maybe's<br /> <br /> <b><u>Kin</u></b><br /> VASCU (like mages)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Not Kin</u></b><br /> Cheiron Group (Cheiron trained Heroes, as mentioned in Slashers; <i>Not Kin unless Slasher; higher than average number of Heroes among their numbers</i>, mission statement includes taking trophys, pieces of monsters, the more unusual the better...)<br /> Les Mystere (Servants of spirits, not inhuman enough)<br /> Knights of St George (from the Faceless Angels)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD Slashers, pg 49</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And among the Aegis Kai Doru a theory has been doing the rounds for years about how the very first slashers, the originators of the slasher phenomenon in fact, were those heroes of myth and legend. Of course, the very first of them was Heracles, who killed beasts, kings, and his own children in his fabled madness: and Heracles\u2019 tutor, the one who taught him to be a \u201chero?\u201d<br /> <i><b>Cheiron.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-05-2015, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T03:13:26-07:00","id":540821,"title":"","content":"The text specifically counts VASCU as not kin. Though but for that, I <i>would</i> regard them as kin, because the Wintergreen process alters them on a deep level. (For the same reason, I might count Ascending Ones, because their bodies are changed so as to accept the Elixirs).<br /> <br /> I'd count Prometheans as kin <i>while</i> they're digesting a mage they sacrificed, but not otherwise (though that's metaphysically kin only; I figure a Beast who knows how they got it would reject the association). Likewise the Cheiron Group if they have implants.<br /> <br /> The magic-using groups - Malleus Maleficarum, Cainite Heresy, Les Mysteres, Knights of St George - maybe their rituals are things anyone could use, like relics or advanced armoury, or maybe they represent a low level change to the spirit, like psychics. In other words, whether or not they're kin should be up to the ST because it has plot implications the other groups don't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:34:33-07:00","id":541075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/539911-mythbreakers-hero-and-the-beast#post539911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally, how do you think Heroes would deal with the Hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to spend some time but I would think the Union would spend equal amounts of time killing off Heroes as well as Beasts.<br /> <br /> Reason being is that the Union cares first and foremost about their lively hood and their places of work. Heroes and Beasts conflicts have a habit of destroying that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Great, you killed the Beast. You just took out the mine that supplied all of our jobs! You know what. Fuck you Hero! Jimmy, get the noose. We'll hang this fucker high today.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:36:15-07:00","id":541170,"title":"","content":"Ashwood would party with Heroes, they are Ashwood after all.<br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule I can't see having any tolerance for a bunch of murderhobos. <br /> <br /> Heroes and Aegis would probably get into conflict, heroes would want magic items, and it's not like Aegis could tell a legitimate magic item and an anethema weapon.<br /> <br /> Cheiron group would be happy to recruit them and cut them up, hey it's Cheiron after all.<br /> <br /> Vanguard would hunt heroes, supernatural serial killers are supernatural serial killers. If a beast is being troublesome they'd probably be willing to get them a work release to help hunt beasts. Vanguard would probably have a program to get heroes psychological help so they can hit integrity 5 and become muggles again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:47:02-07:00","id":541325,"title":"","content":"Would you say Unseen Sense counts as psychic, and thus Kin under the fundamentally human category? If so, a fair number of Keepers of the Source would be kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:23:12-07:00","id":541874,"title":"","content":"Nope. Not enough 'omph', IMO.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't at least make you a Sleepwalker by MtAw 2nd standards and give you some kind of control over it, then it's not enough to make you count as kin. Actually, I'll extend that to most other 'minor' templates (Wolf-Blooded, Purified, Skin-thieves, Ghouls?). Of course as SunlessNick pointed out, it may not apply to all such cases. I missed the part where VASCU was called out as not kin.<br /> <br /> If VASCU aren't kin, then I don't feel that 'the magic-using groups - Malleus Maleficarum, Cainite Heresy, etc' are either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:25:28-07:00","id":542069,"title":"","content":"I could see it, it lists psychics and mediums as kin of the &quot;mostly human variety,&quot; and psychic powers and medium are both supernatural merits, like unseen senses, but yeah that's ST fiat time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:39:32-07:00","id":542402,"title":"","content":"Hmm...it appears that my thoughts on the matter are decidedly off the bell curve. Oh well, if I'm already in the minority I may as well admit to my great heresy:<br /> I would allow the the Slasher &amp; the Hero templates to stack.<br /> Yes, that would mean that some Heroes may read as kin to the Begotten. No, I don't think that is far too cruel; such an antagonist would not be introduced, let alone used, lightly.<br /> <br /> While I await my BBQ, allow me to attempt to give an odd possibility regarding how MM reacts to Beasts. According to &quot;On Monsters: An Unnatural History of Fear&quot;, the medieval mindset explained monsters by claiming that they existed at God's sufferance. Both as a testament to his terrifying power and as an object lesson, that no matter your might you are nothing without the Lord.<br /> Given how the Begotten operate and how heroes are made, I'm inclined to say the MM sees Beasts as a sort of test and may even go out of it's why to recruit &amp; train Heroes. Maybe even teahing them to use holy symbols &amp; relics as Anathema.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:12:26-07:00","id":552633,"title":"","content":"I'd like to believe that the Ascending Ones would be counted as kin due to their work refining their should to accept magical elixirs.<br /> <br /> On another topic, I felt kind of cheated that Beasts didn't have a stenotype regarding Hungers, like they were not worth noticing. IDK about you but Hunters can be pretty tough, esp if they have a good cell behind them and really good Endowments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:07:40-07:00","id":553679,"title":"","content":"With the revision, I can see a good deal of Beasts finding at least common ground with hunters.<br /> <br /> Hell, I can see them <i>working together.</i><br /> <br /> Union: Wait. You know that little demon inside you is amoral and often evil...<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Yep.<br /> <br /> Union: So you restrict it to people who have gotten away with horrible crimes, such as slashers...<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Uh-huh.<br /> <br /> Union: And you got it to stop a CEO from literally getting away with mass murder.<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Long and short of it.<br /> <br /> Union: ...Are you open to the idea of mutual back scratching?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:10:30-07:00","id":553680,"title":"","content":"That'd last until the Beast had eaten most of the major competition and the Local Gaston wondered aloud whether the Beast would come for their kids next. The Union are kind of an ugly, xenophobic group that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:26:40-07:00","id":553835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/539911-mythbreakers-hero-and-the-beast?p=553679#post553679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the revision, I can see a good deal of Beasts finding at least common ground with hunters.<br /> <br /> Hell, I can see them <i>working together.</i><br /> <br /> Union: Wait. You know that little demon inside you is amoral and often evil...<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Yep.<br /> <br /> Union: So you restrict it to people who have gotten away with horrible crimes, such as slashers...<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Uh-huh.<br /> <br /> Union: And you got it to stop a CEO from literally getting away with mass murder.<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Long and short of it.<br /> <br /> Union: ...Are you open to the idea of mutual back scratching?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do the revision make this more likely than before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}